<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        WIRE-FRAUD PREREQUISITE GATE - PHASE 2, ON THE Checklist_Item__c MODEL (design
        agent-output/design-transaction-fsd-gaps.md 5.1, 10). Blocks an item completing while the
        item its Blocked_By__c points at is still open - B3 behind B2, I8 behind I7, and any pair a
        future Transaction_Task_Def__mdt row defines.

        THIS RULE IS THE HALF OF THE CONTROL THAT MUST SHIP IN THIS CHANGE AND NOT BEFORE IT.
        Checklist_Item__c.Is_Prerequisite_Met__c deployed in Phase 1 with its own description
        saying so verbatim: "NO VALIDATION RULE SHIPS IN PHASE 1: with no handler maintaining this
        field, a rule keyed on it would refuse every completion in the org. The rule lands in Phase
        2, in the same change as the handler." ChecklistItemTriggerHandler is that handler and it is
        in this same deploy. Deploying this file WITHOUT it makes every gated item permanently
        uncompletable.

        WHY A VALIDATION RULE AT ALL, GIVEN THE TRIGGER COVERS EVERY WRITE PATH.
        Defence in depth, and the same call this repo already made on Wire__c's
        Verified_DateTime_Not_Backdatable (D-12 = BOTH): a validation rule still evaluates under
        AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE and still evaluates if the trigger is ever deactivated, and it is the
        component that refuses an INSERT created already-complete - a case the trigger deliberately
        does not resolve, because a sibling lookup in the before-insert context would put 21 extra
        SOQL on the fan-out's own insert cascade (the arithmetic is at
        ChecklistItemPrerequisiteService.clampOnInsert). The trigger owns UPDATE; this rule owns the
        INSERT refusal, reading the value clampOnInsert forced to false. The two are NOT redundant
        and must not be collapsed.

        WHY OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(Flag__c)).
        ISCHANGED is FALSE on insert, so an ISCHANGED-only rule would let a data loader or API caller
        INSERT an item pre-set to Completed straight through with no evaluation. ISNEW() closes that.
        Symmetrically, the rule does NOT re-trap an already-complete row for an unrelated later edit
        (a comment, a due date) - only an actual transition into, or an insert directly as, a done
        state is gated. Same reasoning as the Wire__c precedent.

        WHY BOTH Completed AND Verified.
        Flag__c is the single lossy picklist the business chose, and DONE means Completed OR
        Verified. A rule testing Completed alone would let every gated item through by marking it
        Verified instead - which is precisely the value the two wire-verification items use. The
        matching Apex test is ChecklistItemDomain.isDone; the two must move together.

        WHY NOT PRIORVALUE HERE, UNLIKE THE PHASE 0 TASK RULE - STATED PLAINLY RATHER THAN QUIETLY.
        The Task-scoped rule closes the blank-the-key-and-complete bypass declaratively with
        BLANKVALUE(Blocked_By__c, PRIORVALUE(Blocked_By__c)). PRIORVALUE was PROVEN by a check-only
        dry-run to compile on that Text field; on a LOOKUP field at API 67.0 it is UNPROVEN in this
        org, and this repo's standing rule is not to ship an unverified metadata shape as if it were
        proven (see 3.4 of ARCHITECTURE.md for what happens when that shape is guessed). So the
        surviving-value hardening lives ONLY in the trigger here - ChecklistItemPrerequisiteService's
        survivingBlockedBy, which resolves the STORED value while the row is open and additionally
        refuses the disarming save itself. CONSEQUENCE, ACCEPTED AND RECORDED: this rule alone would
        not stop a one-save blank-and-complete; the trigger does, and it is the primary control.
        Anyone who later proves PRIORVALUE on a Lookup at this API version should add the
        surviving-value conjunct here and delete this paragraph.

        errorDisplayField -> Flag__c, the field the user is actually trying to change.
    -->
    <fullName>Prerequisite_Must_Be_Met_To_Complete</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks completing a checklist item while the item named by Blocked_By__c is still open. Backstop to the ChecklistItemTriggerHandler gate, and the sole refusal for an insert created already complete. See the in-file comment.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(Flag__c)),
    OR(ISPICKVAL(Flag__c, &apos;Completed&apos;), ISPICKVAL(Flag__c, &apos;Verified&apos;)),
    NOT(ISBLANK(Blocked_By__c)),
    NOT(Is_Prerequisite_Met__c)
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Flag__c</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>This item cannot be completed until its required prerequisite checklist item (the wire-fraud verification step) has been completed first.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
